## [:< ##

# name  = host-edit.record.field_names
# descr = the editable host record field vocabulary
# return = list

## HOST-SETUP.md 'host record' -- what is OURS to decide, nothing a pin
## already holds.  'ssh' is split into its two scalar halves [ the [user@]host
## and the port ] because the form engine edits scalars and lists, not nested
## maps ; 'transports' stays ONE ordered list
## [ 'transports' : tcp, ssh:<profile>, later relay:<node>, file ].
##
## this list is the single authority three places read :
## host-edit.source.value_set RE-FILTERS submitted fields against it [ the
## read-only trust columns a display-time value_get injects can therefore
## never reach disk ], field_options advertises it, and create_default seeds
## it.

return qw| name addresses link_user ssh ssh_port transports owner owner_key
    roles |;

